# Every line holds an extended regular expression, a tab, and the message that a
# hit reports. A blank line is skipped, and a line that starts with `#` is a
# note. The match is case-insensitive, so write each pattern in lower case. Use
# `\b` to bound a whole word.
#
# A check against this file strips fenced code blocks and inline code spans
# first, so a rule can name the text it forbids by writing that text in
# backticks.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# British spellings. This repo writes American English.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(colour|colours|behaviour|behaviours|serialise|serialised|serialises|honoured|cancelled)\b	Use the American spelling.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slop
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(provenance|leverag(e|es|ed|ing)|utiliz(e|es|ed|ing)|utilis(e|es|ed|ing))\b	Write what the thing is.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inflated adjectives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(crucial|vital|pivotal|paramount|essential|seamless|seamlessly|robust|comprehensive|powerful|cutting-edge|state-of-the-art|world-class|best-in-class|game-changing|meticulous|meticulously|nuanced|holistic|intricate|vibrant)\b	Delete the adjective, or state the measurable fact it stands for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ceremony verbs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(delve|delves|delved|delving|facilitat(e|es|ed|ing)|foster|fosters|fostered|underscor(e|es|ed|ing)|showcas(e|es|ed|ing)|streamlin(e|es|ed|ing)|empower|empowers|empowered|unlock|unlocks|unlocked|elevat(e|es|ed|ing)|embark|embarks|embarked|navigat(e|es|ed|ing)|boasts)\b	Use the plain verb for the action.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Metaphor that reaches for grandeur
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(realm|landscape|tapestry|testament|journey|ecosystem|synergy|synergies)\b	Name the thing directly.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transition filler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
\b(moreover|furthermore|additionally|notably|importantly|arguably|ultimately|effectively|significantly)\b	Delete the transition. Start the sentence with its subject.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chat boilerplate
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(it.s worth noting|worth noting that|that said,|at the end of the day|deep dive|dives? into|when it comes to|plays? an? (crucial|key|vital|critical) role|a testament to|great question|i hope this helps|as an ai)	Delete the filler. State the fact.
\b(myriad|plethora|insights)\b	Delete the filler. State the fact.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The antithesis and the em dash
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
, not\b	Assert the fact directly. Delete the negated half.
, and (not|never) 	Assert the fact directly. Delete the negated half.
\bnot [^.,;]{1,40}(, but |but rather )	Assert the fact directly. Delete the negated half.
\bnot (just|merely|simply|only)	Assert the fact directly. Delete the negated half.
(is|are|was|were) not [^.]{1,40}\. (it|they) (is|are|was|were)	Assert the fact directly. Delete the negated half.
—	Use a comma, a colon, or a period.
